{
  "manufacturer": "Bosch",
  "manufacturer_slug": "bosch",
  "model": "Control Air 5600 - Water to Air (WAZ software)",
  "model_slug": "control-air-5600-water-to-air",
  "aliases": [
    "Control Air 5600",
    "WAZ 1.03",
    "Bosch WSHP DDC",
    "Bosch water source heat pump BACnet",
    "Bosch TT Water to Air"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Water-source heat pump controller",
  "applies_to": "Bosch water-to-air (water source) heat pumps fitted with the Control Air 5600 DDC controller running WAZ zone software.",
  "summary": "The Control Air 5600 is Bosch's factory-mounted DDC controller for water-source heat pumps. It speaks BACnet MS/TP (or BACnet over ARC156, Modbus, N2 and Lon) and exposes occupancy, mode, setpoint, sensor, configuration and alarm points as AV/BV/MSV objects. The same point list also documents Modbus registers and N2/LON equivalents.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet ARC156"
  ],
  "firmware": "WAZ.1.03",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names end in _1 as printed in the points list.",
    "Two names were split across lines in the PDF and were re-joined here: eq_temp_1 (AV 1902) and zs_sen_combo_sel_1 (AV 40).",
    "Many AV points are configuration selectors (input/output assignments); several only matter when that option (economizer, hot gas reheat, VFD, CO2, damper) is installed.",
    "Writable points are those not marked read-only in the list."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Bosch TT - Water to Air Network Integration Points List",
    "doc_number": "WAZ.1.03",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/service/technical_guides/ipl_waz_1_03.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Leave Control Source at its default (BAS Occupancy Command), then command occupied/unoccupied with occupancy_cmd_1 and set the occupied cooling/heating setpoints. Choose the zone temperature source (ZS sensor, remote sensor or BAS value) and, if the BMS supplies the temperature, write bas_sen_val_1. Monitor current_alarm_1, alm_status_1 and the effective zone temperature.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "occupancy_cmd_1",
        "why": "BAS occupied command; 1 enables unit operation"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 15",
        "name": "ctrl_source_1",
        "why": "Occupancy source; 2 = BAS occupancy command (default)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 3",
        "name": "zone_mode_1",
        "why": "Auto / heat / cool / off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 4",
        "name": "occ_clg_stpt_1",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "occ_htg_stpt_1",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 16",
        "name": "sys_status_1",
        "why": "Unoccupied / occupied / fan only / heating / cooling state"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 7",
        "name": "eff_zone_temp_1",
        "why": "Zone temperature in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 17",
        "name": "current_alarm_1",
        "why": "Active alarm code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 24",
        "name": "alm_status_1",
        "why": "Alarm present flag"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set ctrl_source_1 (AV 15) to 2 = BAS Occupancy Command (factory default) and write occupancy_cmd_1 (BV 1) = 1 to occupy the unit. Other sources are a digital input enable, keypad schedule or manual on. The BAS loop enable point (loop_enabled_1, BV 23) must be 1 to allow heating/cooling; it defaults to 1.",
    "heartbeat": "No communication timeout is described. If the BAS temperature source is used and nothing is ever written, the zone temperature defaults to 74 °F; after that the last written value is used indefinitely.",
    "remote_sensors": "Set the compressor control mode (comp_mode_1, AV 64) to 2 = Zone Control - BAS Sensor and write the zone temperature to bas_sen_val_1 (AV 19). BAS humidity goes to bas_rh_sen_val_1 (AV 56) with rh_bas_sel_1 (AV 51); BAS CO2 to bas_co2_val_1 (AV 49) with co2_bas_ena_1 (AV 106); mixed air to bas_mat_1 (AV 86); outdoor air to effective_oat_1 (AV 29).",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP runs on the EIA-485 port; the BAS Port Settings DIP switches select the protocol (BACnet MS/TP, N2, Modbus) and baud rate (9.6 to 76.8 kbps), the same for every controller on the trunk.",
      "The two rotary dials set the MAC address (tens and ones); the controller only reads them at power-up, so change them with power off.",
      "A Communication jumper selects EIA-485 (MS/TP, N2, Modbus, Lon) or BACnet over ARC156 at 156 kbps.",
      "Setpoints and configuration can also be changed locally with a BACview terminal or Virtual BACview."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "With a ZS or remote sensor selected, the controller looks for it during the first 30 s after power-up; if missing, the unit stays unoccupied, alarms and shows -60 °F.",
      "Writing bas_smoke_1 = 1 shuts the supply fan, compressors and reheat valve off.",
      "The input/output configuration AVs (in1/in2/ao/bo cfg) change how hardware I/O is used; treat them as commissioning settings, not operating points.",
      "There is a 1-minute delay when the unit changes between heating and cooling."
    ]
  },
